    <GaugingStation location="Langholm" name="Lugar Water" number="83004">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station in a very responsive, natural and mostly upland catchment.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Rock/boulder control (may be subject to erosion/accretion) plus a thin-plate weir in the mill lade (Langholm B, local no. 140, station level 84.17mOD; closed 1990). Combined flows are archived. Peak flow ratings derived from current meter gaugings up to 1.93m (about 0.5 QMED), simple extrapolation beyond.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity area station; approx. 15m wide.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Flows from Jan 2002 reprocessed in 2012. Icing evident in hydrograph 1-14/1/2011.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Very responsive, natural catchment (open cast mines and minor effluent discharge close to the station).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">A mostly upland catchment developed, mainly, on Carboniferous sediments (chiefly Coal Measures) and igneous formations; extensively overlain by superficial deposits. Hill grazing is the major landuse with some forestry. No significant catchment changes known.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged to near QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="No confidence in estimates for higher flows due to extent of extrapolation above highest gauging and lack of containment in channel." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
